## 2. Core Architectural Pillars (Chimera)

```mermaid
graph TD
    A["Isomorphic JSX Component (.tsx)"] -->|"@frontbase/compiler"| B("Engine Component<br/>(renders everywhere)")
    A -->|"@frontbase/compiler"| D("Component Manifest (Zod)<br/>+ Registered Queries")
    B --> E["Edge Worker<br/>(SEO / first load)"]
    B --> F["Service Worker<br/>(zero-latency nav, offline)"]
    B --> G["Builder Canvas SW<br/>(WYSIWYG preview)"]
    D --> H["Builder Property Panels<br/>+ Agent Diagnostics"]
```

### Pillar 1 — One Engine, Three Environments
The same `@frontbase/edge-core` bundle executes on the cloud edge, inside the browser's service worker, and inside the builder preview. Environment differences are isolated behind a **dependency-injected Data Provider** (`direct` with edge secrets / `proxy` via registered queries / `local draft` SQLite WASM). See [CHIMERA-ARCHITECTURE.md](./CHIMERA-ARCHITECTURE.md) §4.

### Pillar 2 — Zero Component Duplication
Page components are isomorphic Hono/JSX functions rendered to HTML strings. Published pages ship **no React**; interactivity comes from a ~10 KB declarative client-behaviors runtime (`data-fb-*` attributes) — a formalization of the existing `interactive.ts` pattern. React survives only as the builder's own UI shell.

### Pillar 3 — Registered-Query Data Security
The service worker never holds credentials and never sends SQL. The compiler registers every data binding as a named query with a Zod parameter schema; the **Edge Data Proxy** validates auth + params + tenant scope and executes with edge-held secrets.

### Pillar 4 — Single-Worker CMS
The unified Hono router mounts, in priority order: engine/builder static assets → builder SPA shell (`/app/*`) → console API (`/api/console`, from `@frontbase/backend`) → Edge Data Proxy (`/api/data`) → workflows (`/workflows`) → public eSSR catch-all. One deploy, one URL, zero infrastructure.

### Core Framework Scope (@frontbase/edge-core)

**Includes**: Hono unified router & platform adapters; eSSR renderer (isomorphic JSX → HTML string, LiquidJS filters); data-provider DI contract + built-in proxy provider; programmatic Workflow Execution Engine (in-memory defaults, durable via edge-infra adapters); client behaviors runtime; SW synchronization primitives; core types.

**Excludes** (lives elsewhere): compilation/CLI → `@frontbase/compiler`; visual editors & draft DB → `@frontbase/builder`; concrete persistence/proxy/vault/auth-gates/sync → `@frontbase/edge-infra`; console API → `@frontbase/backend`.

