## 3. Current State vs. Proposal Gap Analysis

### ✅ Strong Foundation (Already Exists)

| Area | Current State | Chimera Requirement | Gap / Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Hono Edge Runtime** | Multi-platform Hono serving SSR, workflows, APIs (`lite.ts`/`full.ts`). | Unified single-worker router. | ✅ Exists; needs consolidation into one priority router. |
| **SSR String Renderers** | ~1,600 lines of per-component string builders + LiquidJS (`PageRenderer.ts`). | Isomorphic engine components. | ⚠️ Strong seed — must be generalized to run in SW and be compiler-generated. |
| **Workflow Engine** | `runtime.ts` with queue abstractions, cron, checkpoints. | Programmatic workflows in engine. | ✅ Exists; needs DI provider seam. |
| **Component/Property Registry** | `componentRegistry.tsx` + `propertySchemas.ts` (small but proven pattern). | Zod-driven manifests. | ⚠️ Pattern exists; automation and scale are new. |
| **Monorepo** | 8 `@frontbase/*` data-widget packages. | 6-package framework. | ⚠️ Structure exists; framework packages are new. |

### ❌ Critical Gaps (Must Be Built)

| Area | Missing Capability | Impact |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Compiler** | No AST transformation, schema extraction, query registration, or SW bundle emission. | **BLOCKER** — the build foundation of the Chimera. |
| **Service-Worker Engine Host** | Engine has never run in a SW; no lifecycle/versioning/cache layer. | **BLOCKER** — the defining Chimera capability; Phase 0 validates it. |
| **Data Provider DI + Edge Data Proxy** | Data access is hard-wired; no registered-query proxy. | **HIGH** — security model of the Chimera. |
| **Unified Single-Worker Packaging** | Builder SPA, console API, and engine deploy separately today. | **HIGH** — Principle #1. |
| **CLI Tools** | No `frontbase init/check/lint/simulate/deploy`. | **HIGH** — agent DX. |
| **Console API on Edge** | Console backend is Python/FastAPI (container). | **HIGH** — must be re-implemented as Hono sub-router (`@frontbase/backend`). |

