## 7. Risk Analysis & Mitigation Matrix

| Risk | Severity | Mitigation Strategy |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Engine-in-SW proves impractical** (size, lifecycle, Safari quirks) | **HIGH** | Phase 0 spike validates SW hosting *first*; fallback-by-design means the framework still works as pure edge eSSR if the SW layer is deferred. |
| **Compiler complexity explosion** | **HIGH** | Phase 1 compiler starts with schema extraction + wrapping existing string renderers; TSX→engine codegen lands incrementally. |
| **SW staleness after publish** | **MEDIUM** | Versioned `sw.js` + `skipWaiting()` + manifest revalidation (CHIMERA §7). |
| **Data proxy abuse** | **HIGH** | Registered queries only — no raw SQL from the browser; Zod param validation + tenant scoping at the proxy. |
| **Worker size limits** (1 MB gzip CF free) | **MEDIUM** | Size budgets per package; builder SPA served as static assets, not worker script; CI bundle-size gates. |
| **Breaking existing builder pages** | **CRITICAL** | Layout version flags in DB; edge path renders old layouts via legacy renderer until migrated; feature flags allow instant reversion. |
| **Console API rewrite scope** (FastAPI → Hono) | **MEDIUM** | Scope Phase 2 console to CMS-critical routes (pages, drafts, publish, auth, tenants); long-tail admin routes migrate post-GA. |

