## 8. Implementation Roadmap (Chimera)

> Solo-capacity estimates. Engineering time ≈ 21–27 weeks; calendar target GA **Q1–Q2 2027**. Details in [MILESTONES.md](./MILESTONES.md).

### Phase 0: Chimera Validation Spike (1–2 Weeks, July 2026)
As above.

### Phase 1: Engine & Compiler (8–10 Weeks, Q3 2026)
**Objective**: Extract `@frontbase/edge-core` (the engine) and build `@frontbase/compiler` MVP.
- Engine extraction: unified router, eSSR renderer seeded from existing string renderers, data-provider DI seam, workflows runner with in-memory defaults, client behaviors runtime.
- Compiler MVP: schema extraction, manifest generation, registered-query compilation, SW bundle emission.
- CLI: `init`, `check`, `lint` (JSON diagnostics first); `simulate` after engine stabilizes.
- Target: engine < 70 KB min+gzip; existing published pages render byte-identically through the new engine on the edge path.

### Phase 2: Infra, Console & Builder (6–8 Weeks, Q4 2026)
**Objective**: Complete the single-worker CMS.
- `@frontbase/edge-infra`: direct data providers (D1/Turso/Postgres-Hyperdrive/SQLite), Edge Data Proxy, KV/Redis cache, queues, vault, edge auth gates, sync adapters.
- `@frontbase/backend`: Hono console sub-router (pages, drafts, publish, tenants, tokens) + Drizzle schemas/migrations — mounted in the same worker; zero Python in the deploy.
- `@frontbase/builder`: React shell extraction, local SQLite WASM draft DB, canvas↔SW preview bridge, visual workflow & sync editors.
- Single-worker packaging + `frontbase deploy`.

### Phase 3: Agent Experience (3–4 Weeks, Q1 2027)
- Diagnostic refinement: quick-fixes, contextual errors, enhanced JSON.
- Tri-environment simulation checks; agent prompt templates; beta program (20+ testers).

### Phase 4: GA Launch (2–3 Weeks, Q1–Q2 2027)
- Documentation, launch materials, support channels, public release.

